      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T20:35:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could a FP from a blender just always have two children (src and dst) and then if we need the actual dest color from the framebuffer we just bind a child FP to dst that provides it?",
      "revId": "ccfadd3a05ec735ad748bed086aad06300f33b84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7b20124_be2b0bbc",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T20:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is exactly how it does work, actually! See \nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/gpu/SkGr.cpp;l\u003d517;drc\u003da6648599b594d225f5020d6c7428dcec41439934\n\nWhen your SkPaint has a blender on it, the `src` is the paintFP up until that point, and the `dst` is GrFragmentProcessor::DestColor. And that\u0027s how blenders work on the GrPaint right now.\n\nThe only time FPs *won\u0027t* be bound to both src and dst is when Runtime Effect SkSL directly calls `sample(blender, x, y)`. In that case src and dst should be used exactly as provided. I am working on adding that support now. These changes are prep work to allow for that use case.",
      "parentUuid": "0ce796f5_28ae0d52",
      "revId": "ccfadd3a05ec735ad748bed086aad06300f33b84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb7e348e_de724f64",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T20:58:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, so x, y here are arbitrary colors computed in the caller, right?\n\nWe have most FPs that don\u0027t use the single input color that is always there, a few that do, and now we\u0027re going to have some that use two inputs. I\u0027m wondering if we really should be thinking about some new model of FPs with a more flexible call signature.",
      "parentUuid": "f7b20124_be2b0bbc",
      "revId": "ccfadd3a05ec735ad748bed086aad06300f33b84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d6035c3c_7c9a8523",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T21:05:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"x,y are arbitrary colors computed in the caller\": Yes, exactly.\n\n\"flexible call signature\": Without a doubt. Finding and plumbing through an additional call signature throughout the various affected spots in Gr has been difficult and it would be nice to be able to say that it\u0027s a solved problem forever. It would be awesome if we had a more flexible model that supported arbitrary argument lists. Obviously this opens up a ton of unanswered questions, but it\u0027s definitely worth thinking about. Especially if we can imagine more types of sample-able things besides shaders, color filters and blenders.",
      "parentUuid": "fb7e348e_de724f64",
      "revId": "ccfadd3a05ec735ad748bed086aad06300f33b84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
